.TH CONSUMEROSCTL 1 "2026-08-07" "ConsumerOS 1.0" "ConsumerOS commands"
.SH NAME
consumerosctl \- inspect and control ConsumerOS services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B consumerosctl
.RI [ --compact ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B consumerosctl
is the validated JSON control interface used by ConsumerOS System Hub. Read-only
commands report system, hardware, update, compatibility, feature, snapshot, and
recovery state. Mutating commands require administrator authorization.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report system readiness, protection, storage, desktop, and update state.
.TP
.B hardware
Report graphics, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio, camera, controller, and printing support.
.TP
.B update
Check, stage, apply, cancel, inspect, or select a stable/current update channel.
.TP
.B drivers
Recommend and install repository drivers or inspect and apply firmware updates.
.TP
.B snapshots
List, create, and select Btrfs system restore points.
.TP
.B recovery
Run diagnostics or explicit repair operations.
.TP
.B feature
List, enable, or disable optional ConsumerOS capability profiles.
.TP
.B compatibility
Look up or search the local application compatibility database.
.SH SECURITY
Use System Hub for normal operation. Privileged commands validate their actions
and targets but can change the installed operating system.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.offline-updates (7),
.BR snapper (8),
.BR flatpak (1)
